# Documentation Discipline

For behavior-changing code or configuration changes, review whether docs must change. Use `docs/domains/README.md` to pick the owning domain doc instead of loading the whole docs tree.

Always consider:

- `docs/core/CURRENT_STATE.md` for current implementation status
- `docs/core/DECISIONS.md` for durable decisions
- `docs/core/ARCHITECTURE.md` for service/artifact boundary changes
- `docs/governance/DEFERRED_WORK.md` for postponed concerns
- `docs/sprints/README.md` for sprint status changes

If no documentation update is needed, say why in the final summary.
